Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 19 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.214
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.214 V18.4.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Media-Component-Status (549): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.48
  Callee-Information (565): Grouped, 3 members, clause 5.3.62
  FLUS-Identifier (566): OctetString, clause 5.3.63
  Desired-Max-Latency (567): Float32, clause 5.3.64
  Desired-Max-Loss (568): Float32, clause 5.3.65
  NID (569): OctetString, clause 5.3.68
  MA-Information (570): Grouped, 3 members, clause 5.3.66
  MA-Information-Action (571): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.67
  5GS-RAN-NAS-Release-Cause (572): Grouped, 3 members, clause 5.3.69
  5GMM-Cause (573): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.70
  5GSM-Cause (574): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.71
  NGAP-Cause (575): Grouped, 2 members, clause 5.3.72
  NGAP-Group (576): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.73
  NGAP-Value (577): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.74
  Wireline-User-Location-Info (578): Grouped, 3 members, clause 5.3.75
  HFC-Node-Identifier (579): OctetString, clause 5.3.76
  GLI-Identifier (580): OctetString, clause 5.3.77
  Line-Type (581): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.78
  MPS-Action (582): Enumerated, 4 values, clause 5.3.79

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
